CPU

The CPU (Central Processing Unit) handles the main calculations and instructions needed to run the game. 
It manages tasks such as game logic, player movements, physics, and communication between different hardware components.

RAM

RAM (Random Access Memory) temporarily stores the game’s data and instructions that the CPU needs to access quickly.
More RAM helps the game run smoothly and reduces slowdowns when other programs are running in the background.

GPU

The GPU (Graphics Processing Unit) is responsible for rendering the game’s graphics, including characters, environments, textures, and visual effects.
A stronger GPU can provide higher graphics quality and smoother gameplay with better FPS (frames per second).
